{%- comment -%} Styles live in assets/ha-sections.css, loaded once in layout/theme.liquid. {%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Hartwick Atelier — THE MASTER (product page).
  Aloha, 16 September 2026:

    "The Master section introduces the person or workshop responsible for
     making the selected garment or its cloth. […] A large photograph of the
     relevant Master working, their hands, loom or workshop. Their name
     positioned over the photograph. Their discipline and location — what they
     contributed and where. 'View Master Record' linking to their dedicated
     page […] each product should reference the appropriate Master record so
     the photograph, name and link come from that shared record."

  So this section holds NO content of its own. It reads the first `master`
  record in hartwick.masters (falling back to the product's Lot's masters),
  and prints that record's workshop photograph, name, discipline and place,
  and a link to the record's own page — `master.system.url` once the
  metaobject definition has storefront pages switched on, else the Masters
  index page chosen below. The photograph may be overridden per section only
  as a stand-in; the record wins the moment it carries an image.

  HONESTY (CLAUDE.md, and the brief: "Do not connect a generic artisan
  photograph to this product without confirming the relationship and image
  permission"). A record with no name renders the design's labelled slot —
  "[Master name]", "[Discipline] / [Place]", "Workshop photograph / to supply",
  "Identity + product link to verify" — never a role dressed as a person and
  never a photograph that has not been tied to this garment. The cross-hairs
  in the artboard are a design annotation for the empty slot and are drawn
  here for the same reason, so the slot cannot be mistaken for finished art.

  THE MASTER'S TOOL (Aloha, 23 September 2026): "On each individual product
  page, please feature the master's handcrafted tools that our products
  highlight. For example, if a shirt is labeled as handspun, we should
  showcase the master's handspun tool." Each `tool` block pairs a technique
  with the photograph of its tool from the Masters shoot — the same frames
  the Masters page glossary uses (charkha for hand spun, the loom's warp for
  handwoven, a carved block's face for block printing, dyed bobbins for
  natural dye). The product's own label is read in the order a visitor
  reads it — Expression ("Handspun Silk & Linen"), the material line
  ("HANDSPUN / HANDWOVEN"), the process tags, the old site's process marks,
  the title — and the tool whose word comes FIRST wins, so a handspun shirt
  shows the charkha and a block print shows the block.
  The tool is shown as a tool, never as a person: with no verified Master
  the heading is the tool's name, not a name slot. A verified Master keeps
  their name; the tool photograph then stands in only while their record
  has no image of its own.

  Composition (V2): a dark full-bleed band ~1040px tall at 1500 wide; eyebrow
  top-left, the photograph's caption top-right, the name and
  discipline / place bottom-left over the image, the link beneath a short rule.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign mf = product.metafields.hartwick
  assign master = mf.masters.value.first
  if master == blank
    assign master = mf.lot.value.masters.value.first
  endif

  assign m_name = master.name.value
  assign m_role = master.role.value
  assign m_place = master.region.value.place
  if master.region.value.region != blank and m_place != blank
    assign m_place = m_place | append: ', ' | append: master.region.value.region
  elsif master.region.value.region != blank
    assign m_place = master.region.value.region
  endif

  assign has_identity = false
  if m_name != blank
    assign has_identity = true
  endif

  # --- the tool: the technique whose word comes first in the product's label
  capture label
    render 'ha-product-fact', product: product, field: 'expression'
    echo ' | '
    render 'ha-product-fact', product: product, field: 'material_line'
    echo ' | '
    echo mf.process_tags
    for i in (1..4)
      assign key = 'process_' | append: i
      assign mark = product.metafields.custom[key].value
      if mark != blank
        echo ' | '
        echo mark.title.value
      endif
    endfor
    echo ' | '
    echo product.title
  endcapture
  assign label = label | upcase
  assign tool = nil
  assign tool_pos = 100000
  for block in section.blocks
    if block.type != 'tool' or block.settings.image == blank
      continue
    endif
    assign words = block.settings.match | upcase | split: ','
    for w in words
      assign w = w | strip
      if w == blank
        continue
      endif
      unless label contains w
        continue
      endunless
      assign pos = label | split: w | first | size
      if pos < tool_pos
        assign tool_pos = pos
        assign tool = block
      endif
    endfor
  endfor

  assign photo = master.workshop_images.value.first | default: master.portrait.value
  assign photo_alt = section.settings.photo_alt
  if has_identity == false
    assign photo = nil
  endif
  assign photo_is_tool = false
  if photo == blank and tool != blank
    assign photo_is_tool = true
    assign photo = tool.settings.image
    assign photo_alt = tool.settings.alt | default: tool.settings.name
  endif
  if photo == blank and has_identity and section.settings.standin_image != blank
    assign photo = section.settings.standin_image
  endif

  assign tool_href = ''
  if tool != blank and section.settings.masters_page != blank
    assign tool_href = section.settings.masters_page.url
    if tool.settings.anchor != blank
      assign tool_href = tool_href | append: '#' | append: tool.settings.anchor
    endif
  endif

  assign href = ''
  if master.system.url != blank
    assign href = master.system.url
  elsif section.settings.masters_page != blank
    assign href = section.settings.masters_page.url
    if master.system.handle != blank
      assign href = href | append: '#' | append: master.system.handle
    endif
  endif

  assign number = section.settings.number | default: '01'
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  Tab 05 (16 September): "Hide unverified maker module until confirmed."
  With no verified Master the section renders nothing — unless "Show the
  empty slot" is on, which it is on the development theme so Aloha can check
  the placement. Untick it before publishing and the module disappears from
  every garment that has no verified Master, and returns by itself when one
  is linked.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign show_tool = false
  if has_identity == false and tool != blank
    assign show_tool = true
  endif
-%}
{%- if has_identity or show_tool or section.settings.show_slot -%}
<section class="ha-section ha-section--field-peat ha-masterfeat{% if photo != blank %} ha-masterfeat--photo{% endif %}{% if show_tool %} ha-masterfeat--tool{% elsif has_identity == false %} ha-masterfeat--slot{% endif %}"{% if tool != blank %} data-tool="{{ tool.settings.anchor | escape }}"{% endif %}>
  {%- if photo != blank -%}
    <div class="ha-masterfeat__media">
      {{ photo
        | image_url: width: 2800
        | image_tag:
          loading: 'lazy',
          sizes: '100vw',
          widths: '750, 1100, 1500, 2000, 2800',
          alt: photo_alt,
          class: 'ha-masterfeat__img' }}
      <span class="ha-masterfeat__scrim" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </div>
  {%- else -%}
    <div class="ha-masterfeat__slotmarks" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></div>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="ha-wrap ha-masterfeat__grid">
    <p class="ha-eyebrow ha-identify ha-masterfeat__eyebrow">
      {%- if show_tool -%}{{ section.settings.tool_eyebrow }}{%- else -%}{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}{%- endif %} / {{ number }}</p>

    <p class="ha-masterfeat__slotlabel ha-record">
      {%- if photo_is_tool -%}
        {{ tool.settings.caption }}
      {%- elsif photo != blank and section.settings.photo_caption != blank -%}
        {{ section.settings.photo_caption }}
      {%- elsif photo == blank -%}
        {{ section.settings.slot_photo_label }}
      {%- endif -%}
    </p>

    <div class="ha-masterfeat__identity">
      <h2 class="ha-masterfeat__name ha-narrate">
        {%- if has_identity -%}{{ m_name }}{%- elsif show_tool -%}{{ tool.settings.name }}{%- else -%}{{ section.settings.slot_name }}{%- endif -%}
      </h2>
      <p class="ha-masterfeat__line ha-record">
        {%- if show_tool -%}
          {{ tool.settings.technique }}{% if tool.settings.line != blank %} / {{ tool.settings.line }}{% endif %}
        {%- elsif has_identity -%}
          {{ m_role | default: section.settings.slot_discipline }} / {{ m_place | default: section.settings.slot_place }}
        {%- else -%}
          {{ section.settings.slot_discipline }} / {{ section.settings.slot_place }}
        {%- endif -%}
      </p>
      <hr class="ha-masterfeat__rule">
      {%- if has_identity and href != blank -%}
        <a class="ha-masterfeat__link ha-record" href="{{ href }}">{{ section.settings.link_text }}<span class="ha-pdp__arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span></a>
      {%- elsif show_tool and tool_href != blank -%}
        <a class="ha-masterfeat__link ha-record" href="{{ tool_href }}">{{ section.settings.tool_link_text }}<span class="ha-pdp__arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span></a>
      {%- elsif show_tool -%}
      {%- else -%}
        <span class="ha-masterfeat__link ha-masterfeat__link--inert ha-record" aria-disabled="true">{{ section.settings.link_text }}<span class="ha-pdp__arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span></span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- if show_tool -%}
      {%- render 'ha-placeholder-note', show: section.settings.show_placeholder_note,
        text: 'No named Master is linked to this garment yet, so the section shows the tool of its first technique (matched from the product label). A Master linked in hartwick.masters takes this place with their name.' -%}
    {%- elsif has_identity == false -%}
      <p class="ha-masterfeat__verify ha-record">{{ section.settings.slot_verify }}</p>
      {%- render 'ha-placeholder-note', show: section.settings.show_placeholder_note,
        text: 'No Master is linked to this garment yet — the slot publishes from the master record in hartwick.masters (name, discipline, place, workshop photograph, record link).' -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "HA — The Master",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "ha-section-wrapper",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Reads the first Master linked to this product (hartwick.masters). Nothing about the person is typed here." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "The Master" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "number", "label": "Number", "default": "01" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "link_text", "label": "Link text", "default": "View Master Record" },
    { "type": "page", "id": "masters_page", "label": "Masters page", "info": "Used for the link until the master record has its own page (metaobject storefront pages)." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Photograph" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "photo_caption", "label": "Caption (top right)" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "photo_alt", "label": "Alt text" },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "standin_image", "label": "Stand-in photograph", "info": "Shown only while the record has no image, no tool matches AND a name is verified. Never shown for an unnamed record." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "The Master's tool", "info": "Aloha, 23 Sept: feature the tool of the technique the product is labelled with. Add one Tool block per technique; the first matching word in the product's label wins." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "tool_eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow when a tool is shown", "default": "The Master's Tool" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "tool_link_text", "label": "Tool link text", "default": "Visit The Masters" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "The empty slot (design annotations)" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "slot_photo_label", "label": "Photo slot label", "default": "Workshop photograph / to supply" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "slot_name", "label": "Name slot", "default": "[Master name]" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "slot_discipline", "label": "Discipline slot", "default": "[Discipline]" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "slot_place", "label": "Place slot", "default": "[Place]" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "slot_verify", "label": "Verify note", "default": "Identity + product link to verify" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_slot", "label": "Show the empty slot when no Master is verified", "default": false, "info": "Off = the module is hidden until a Master is linked (sheet, tab 05). On for layout checks." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_placeholder_note", "label": "Show placeholder notice", "default": true }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "tool",
      "name": "Tool",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "technique", "label": "Technique", "default": "Hand spun" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "match", "label": "Label words that select it", "default": "handspun, hand spun, hand-spun", "info": "Comma-separated, any case. Matched against the Expression, material line, process tags, old process marks and title." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "name", "label": "Tool name (heading)", "default": "The Charkha" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "line", "label": "Line beneath", "default": "From fibre to yarn" },
        { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Photograph of the tool" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "alt", "label": "Alt text" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "caption", "label": "Caption (top right)" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "anchor", "label": "Masters page entry", "default": "hand-spun", "info": "The glossary key on The Masters page — the link opens that entry." }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "HA — The Master" }]
}
{% endschema %}
